{#
  The prompt a Claude session starts with (`ergon work`), for one task or
  several taken on together.

  Every task comes as its intent split in two: `title`, its first line, and
  `body`, the rest (empty when there is none).

  ancestors   every task's ancestors, merged, in tree order from the root,
              each also with `pad`: two spaces per level below the root
  tasks       the tasks to complete, in tree order, each also with
                reference   e.g. demo/E6dn
                subtasks    its non-cancelled subtree, depth-first, each
                            also with
                  pad      two spaces per level below the task
                  marker   "done", "landing", or null

  choros_here what `choros here` printed in the session's folder, or
              null when choros isn't installed or that folder isn't in a
              choros space
  bound       whether that folder is a workspace `ergon work` made for
              the tasks, whose lands move them

  `text | indent(with=PREFIX)` puts PREFIX before every non-blank line.

  Tags are indented by nesting and open with `{%-`, which drops the
  indentation and the line break before the tag, so a tag's line prints
  nothing. A blank line goes after a tag: one before it is dropped too.
#}## Context

These are the ancestor tasks which may help frame your work:
{# a blank line before the outline #}
{%- for a in ancestors %}
{{ a.pad }}- {{ a.title }}
  {%- if a.body %}
{{ a.body | indent(with=a.pad ~ "  ") }}
  {%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for task in tasks %}

## Your Task{% if tasks | length > 1 %} {{ loop.index }} of {{ tasks | length }}{% endif %} ({{ task.reference }})

{{ task.title }}
  {%- if task.body %}

{{ task.body }}
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if task.subtasks %}
{# a blank line before the outline #}
    {%- for t in task.subtasks %}
{{ t.pad }}- {% if t.marker %}[{{ t.marker }}] {% endif %}{{ t.title }}
      {%- if t.body %}
{{ t.body | indent(with=t.pad ~ "  ") }}
      {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
  {%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}

## Ergon

These are ergon tasks; change them with the `ergon` CLI (`ergon help` lists
its commands, `ergon tree` shows each task's reference). As the work goes:

{%- if bound %}

- `choros land` from this workspace sets these tasks' statuses; don't set
  them to landing yourself.
- `ergon work` resumes this session only from the folder it began in, so
  don't move that folder, and archive it only with `choros land archive`.
{%- else %}

- Once all of a task's work is landed or in PRs, set it to landing:
  `ergon edit REF --status landing`.
- Until then, leave it in_progress, and set each subtask whose work is all
  landed or in PRs to landing.
- Name the task references (like {{ tasks.0.reference }}) in each PR's title or body.
- `ergon work` resumes this session only from the folder it began in, so
  don't move or archive that folder.
{%- endif %}
{%- if choros_here %}

## Choros

This session's folder is in a choros space. `choros here` says:

```
{{ choros_here }}
```

`choros help agent` says how to work in it.
  {%- if bound %} This workspace is bound to
{% if tasks | length > 1 %}these tasks{% else %}this task{% endif %}: each `choros land` from it tells ergon what it lands.

- `choros land continue` lands a piece. The workspace stays and the task
  stays in_progress, even if the land names it with `--label`. Name a
  subtask the piece finishes with `--label`, by its reference as
  `ergon tree` shows it, and it is set to landing, unless work under it is
  still open.
- `choros land archive` ends the work: it lands what is left, if anything
  is, and sets the task to landing. Run it once the work is done, even with
  everything landed already. It is refused while a subtask is still todo or
  in_progress. The workspace is archived once this session closes;
  `ergon work` then opens the set's landing folder, where review fixes go.

Don't run `choros archive` on this workspace.
  {%- else %} Pass each task a land carries to
`choros land` as `--label`, by its reference (like
`--label {{ tasks.0.reference }}`): `ergon show` finds a land's tasks by these
labels. If this session began in a choros workspace, don't run
`choros land archive` or `choros archive` on it.
  {%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

